## Context

PR #597 established the pattern: plain `[plain]` figure frame → titled analytical companion
with the key finding in the title.

Four plain frames in `slides/slides.tex` still lack titled companions:
- `fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` (line 104) — Exp1 per-model recall performance
- `fig_spider_exp1_claude.pdf` (line 188) — Claude quality dimensions spider
- `fig_spider_exp1_families.pdf` (line 194) — Family-level quality dimensions spider
- `fig_exp2_coverage_certainty.pdf` (line 300) — Coverage vs corroboration scatter

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each of the four plain frames above has a `\begin{frame}{Key finding}` companion
- [ ] Titles are evidence-grounded (data checked before writing)
- [ ] `make check` passes
